  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "A device consists of eight balls, each of mass \\textbf{M} = 6 \\textbf{kg}, attached to the ends of low-mass spokes of length  \\textbf{L} = 1.2 \\textbf{m}, so the radius of rotation of the balls is \\textbf{L/2}. The device is mounted in the vertical plane, as shown in the figure. The axle is held up by supports that are not shown, and the device rotates on the nearly frictionless axle. A lump of clay with mass \\textbf{m} = 3 \\textbf{kg} strikes at the bottom ball at an angle $\\mathbf{\\theta}$ = $25^\\circ$, and sticks to it. Just before the impact the clay has a speed \\textbf{v} = 5 \\textbf{m/s}, and the device is rotating \\textbf{counterclockwise} with angular speed $\\mathbf{\\omega}$ = 0.5 \\textbf{rad/s}",
